                <pb facs="0751" n="743" sameAs="frus:frus1941v03/pg743"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/12158: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-06-17T19:00:00+02:00">June 17, 1941—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 17—12:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2500. My 2499, June 17, 6 p.m.,<anchor n="8" xml:id="d787-f1"/> and Beirut’s 198,
                    June 8. I have communicated the substance of Beirut’s telegram orally to the
                    Foreign Office and when I saw Mr, Eden last evening he asked me to say how very
                    much the;British Government appreciates the attitude and help of Mr. Engert.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
